  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting human rights defenders in Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will support environmental human rights defenders, their organisations and communities affected by extractive projects in Cusco, Apur&#xed;mac, Puno, Cajamarca, Aqeuipa, Pasco, Amazonia and others. Red Muqui in articulation with its members and other organisations and networks will support defenders who face criminalisation, stigmatisation, attacks and threats for protecting our common home and human rights in the face of extractive megaprojects and others, and also in the context of exercising their right to peaceful social protest to vindicate their demands. In the first year, this will be done through trainings, exchanges and networking to develop recommendations and public and communication campaigns and advocacy activities to improve their protection and support, focusing also on the need to ratify the Escazu Agreement in Peru and support for the National Campaign for Environmental Defenders. During 2023, the focus will be on accompanying organisations and communities whose human rights have been violated, especially those criminalised, injured or killed in the context of the social mobilisations linked to the political and social crisis at the end of 2022 and 2023.</narrative>
  </description>
